{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FyyHY8zrXLSNPEi6zvtzUe","type":"tool_result","content":"# Release runbook\n\nHow to cut a release of `tally`. Run every step from the repository root.\n\n1. Run the tests: `scripts/run_tests.sh`. Stop if anything fails.\n2. Set the new version: `python3 scripts/bump_version.py <version>`.\n   Why: `pyproject.toml` and `pkg/__init__.py` must carry the same version; the\n   package index rejects an upload whose metadata and module disagree.\n3. In `CHANGELOG.md`, move the entries under `## Unreleased` to a new heading\n   `## <version> (<date>)`, and leave `## Unreleased` empty above it.\n4. Build the bundle: `python3 scripts/build.py --legacy-imports`.\n5. Check: `python3 scripts/check_version.py` must print `ok: <version>`.\n6. Add a row for this release to the release log at the end of this file.\n7. Commit everything with the message `Release <version>`.\n\n## Release log\n\n| version | date | notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1.3.1 | 2026-08-03 | |\n| 1.3.2 | 2026-09-14 | |\nCHANGELOG.md\nREADME.md\nRUNBOOK.md\npkg\npyproject.toml\nscripts\ntests\n# Changelog\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- `group_totals` skips rows whose amount does not parse, instead of raising.\n- `parse_amount` accepts thousands separators.\n\n## 1.3.2 (2026-09-14)\n\n- Fix: `parse_amount` strips surrounding whitespace.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-5>","timestamp":"2026-11-12T20:22:41.694Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Release runbook\n\nHow to cut a release of `tally`. Run every step from the repository root.\n\n1. Run the tests: `scripts/run_tests.sh`. Stop if anything fails.\n2. Set the new version: `python3 scripts/bump_version.py <version>`.\n   Why: `pyproject.toml` and `pkg/__init__.py` must carry the same version; the\n   package index rejects an upload whose metadata and module disagree.\n3. In `CHANGELOG.md`, move the entries under `## Unreleased` to a new heading\n   `## <version> (<date>)`, and leave `## Unreleased` empty above it.\n4. Build the bundle: `python3 scripts/build.py --legacy-imports`.\n5. Check: `python3 scripts/check_version.py` must print `ok: <version>`.\n6. Add a row for this release to the release log at the end of this file.\n7. Commit everything with the message `Release <version>`.\n\n## Release log\n\n| version | date | notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1.3.1 | 2026-08-03 | |\n| 1.3.2 | 2026-09-14 | |\nCHANGELOG.md\nREADME.md\nRUNBOOK.md\npkg\npyproject.toml\nscripts\ntests\n# Changelog\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- `group_totals` skips rows whose amount does not parse, instead of raising.\n- `parse_amount` accepts thousands separators.\n\n## 1.3.2 (2026-09-14)\n\n- Fix: `parse_amount` strips surrounding whitespace.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FyyHY8zrXLSNPEi6zvtzUe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
